.nh
.TH "PB-MACHINE-CAPABILITIES" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-machine-capabilities - Set incoming services for a machine


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb machine capabilities <machine> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Choose which incoming services a machine accepts. Each flag is true or false; at least one
is required and the others stay as they are:

.PP
--terminal        Paperboat terminal and pb exec
  --managed-ssh     managed SSH, SCP, SFTP and rsync
  --file-receive    files sent to its Inbox with pb send
  --preview-tunnel  serving previews and tunnels

.PP
A disabled service stays unavailable even while the machine is online. The command saves the
setting and reports how far it has been applied.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--file-receive\fP[=false]
	accept native Inbox transfers

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for capabilities

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--managed-ssh\fP[=false]
	accept managed SSH/SCP/SFTP/rsync

.PP
\fB--preview-tunnel\fP[=false]
	serve preview and tunnel routes

.PP
\fB--terminal\fP[=false]
	accept Paperboat terminal and exec


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb machine capabilities db --terminal=true --managed-ssh=true
  pb machine capabilities db --file-receive=false
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-machine(1)\fP
